// Deal or Force - where the panels sit.
//
// Four anchors as fractions of the screen and four offsets in pixels from them, in Godot's
// own terms: left, top, right, bottom. Anchors and offsets are independent, so a mod that
// only wants the army panel forty pixels wider writes `offsets` and inherits `anchors`.
//
// This is the half of the interface a layout mod wants and the reason it is not in
// `interface/`: colour and position are edited by different people for different reasons.
// Every file in this folder is read in name order and later files win.
//
// Only placement is data. What goes inside a panel is still code - a layout file cannot
// invent a new screen - but everything the base game builds can be moved, resized or
// pushed to the other side of the map without touching it.
